==English==

===Etymology===
A borrowing of {{der|en|fr|tellurique}}, from {{der|en|la|tellus|t=[[earth]]; [[earthy]]}} and {{m|la|Tellus|t=[[Earth]], [[Gaia]]}} and {{m|fr|-ique|pos=forming adjectives}}. Subsequently also from {{m|en|tellurium}}, originally in ''telluric oxide'' from {{der|en|de|Telluroxyd}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Pertaining to the Earth, [[earthly]]
#: {{syn|en|earthly|terrestrial|tellurian|terrene}}
#* '''1981''', Italo Calvino, ''If on a Winter's Night a Traveler'':
#*: My sister always says she loves novels where you feel an elemental strength, primordial, '''telluric'''.
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} Containing [[tellurium]] in a lower [[valency]] than in [[tellurous]] compounds.

